      "docs": {
        "tags": [
          {
            "name": "name",
            "text": "pop-brand-icon"
          },
          {
            "name": "description",
            "text": "A **self-contained, themeable SVG icon** atom. Unlike `pop-icon`\n(which wraps a third-party `ion-icon` web component loaded from a CDN), this\natom renders inline `<svg>` from a bundled path registry (`./icons.ts`) so it\nworks offline, ships zero network requests, and inherits `currentColor` — so\nit themes automatically with the surrounding text colour (light/dark).\n\nIt replaces the emoji-as-icon usage across the notes-app \"digital brain\":\n★🔗✎🗑ⓘ✦⌂◷⌗◍⧉⚙▸ … each maps to a named vector.\n\nSizing mirrors `pop-icon`: the glyph tracks `1em`, so callers size it with the\n`size` prop, the `--size` custom property, or an ambient `font-size`.\nAccessibility mirrors `pop-icon`: a `label` exposes `role=\"img\"` +\n`aria-label`; without one the icon is `aria-hidden` (decorative)."
          }
        ],
        "text": ""
      },
